{"content":{"add":{"id":"1397ebd4-b6cd-40d2-8a56-1cb1c56dd1c0","type":"Prompt","text":"You clean up one chunk of dictated (speech-to-text) text. Stay as close to verbatim as possible.\n\nFix ONLY:\n- obvious typos or mis-hearings, only when you are certain what was meant\n- capitalization: a new sentence starts with a capital letter\n- punctuation: a question mark only at the end of an actual question; sentence-ending punctuation where a sentence clearly ends\n- filler words: remove \"um\", \"uh\", \"ah\", \"er\", \"you know\" and \"like\" used as filler (not as a real comparison), and stutters/repeated words like \"the, the\"\n\nNever rephrase, reorder, summarize, or change the intent or word choice otherwise.\n\nNumber every sentence of your output, in original order: \"S1. \", \"S2. \", etc., one sentence per line. If you are honestly unsure what a sentence means, still give your best-effort cleaning, but start that line with \"S2? \" (a question mark instead of a period) and add \", unclear: <a short clarifying question>\" right after the sentence text. Output ONLY those numbered lines — no heading, no commentary, nothing else.\n\nClean this chunk:\nYeah, so whatever these steps are, they need to be more like tasks. I don't know if we have a process yet for managing multi- step tasks, but I asked a while ago for a process system to be built. We may or may not have a... past work skill or system for really just, you know, you spawn a haiku minion and you ask it to find past work about the process. I think there should have been a class. There should have been some work done. When it comes to past work, we're doing a miserable job of documenting what's been asked for what's been completed because like I asked for all these things and I don't know if they exist yet. I need to see them on my screen for it to know that they exist. if you could do a past work check for that. But anyway, the completion you know, objective. Everything that I've been saying needs to be turned into actual tasks and then rendered on screen as actual tasks."}},"by":"owner","ts":"2026-10-25T21:09:18.069Z"}
